# The recipes. ONE LINE PER RECIPE, AND EACH LINE IS ITS OWN DOCUMENT.
#
# A recipe is not a chapter. Unlike docs/manual/ORDER -- which declares the sequence of chapters
# that are concatenated into one book -- nothing here is joined to anything. tools/build-docs.sh
# reads this file and renders each line on its own, to a PDF sitting beside its Markdown and
# carrying the same basename: cpm-from-scratch.md -> cpm-from-scratch.pdf. The package ships the
# folder with the PDFs in it.
#
# SO THE ORDER IS ALPHABETICAL, and that is all it is. There is no first recipe and no last one;
# a reader opens the one whose name is what they want to do. Keep the list sorted so that adding
# one is obvious and nobody has to wonder where it goes.
#
# THE LIST IS STILL LOAD-BEARING. tests/acceptance/docs-manual.cmake fails if a .md in this
# folder is missing from this file -- a recipe that is written, committed and never rendered is
# worse than one that does not exist, because everything looks fine.

cpm-from-scratch.md
dazzler-from-scratch.md
from-a-builtin.md
